========================================
PART 4 — GET THE DATA READY (your 9 Parquet files in R2)
========================================

Your raw files (9 Parquet files of about 285 MB, about 3 GB in total) stay in
the ored-datasets bucket. Below:

FOLDER   = the folder they are in, as step 11 shows it (e.g. training data/)
VERSION  = v1 the first time; v2, v3, ... every time the set of files changes

Use the quotes around FOLDER when it has a space.

---

11. See Your Files in R2

Step 9 first.

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-list

OUTPUT

    0.278 GiB  training data/part-00000.parquet
    0.278 GiB  training data/part-00001.parquet
    ...
9 file(s), 2.5 GiB in r2://ored-datasets/

---

12. Look Inside a File

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-inspect "training data/part-00000.parquet"

(use one of the names step 11 printed)

OUTPUT

"file_format": "parquet",
"parquet_rows": ...,
"parquet_schema": [
  "id: string",
  "text: string",
  ...
],

Only the end of the file (its schema) is downloaded, about 1 MB. Write down:

TEXT_FIELD = the field with the document text (above: text)
ID_FIELD   = the field with the document id (above: id)

---

13. Download the Files

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-fetch --prefix "training data/" --out data\raw\training-data

Parquet files are used as they are (no unpacking). Files already downloaded are
skipped, so you can run it again after adding files.

Needs free disk: about 3 GB for the files + about 2–3 GB for the shards (step 15).

---

14. Train the Tokenizer (once)

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py train-tokenizer --input data\raw\training-data --text-field TEXT_FIELD --vocab-size 16384 --max-bytes 300000000 --name ored-bpe-16k --version v1 --out data\tokenizers\ored-bpe-16k-v1.json

It learns from a 300 MB sample spread over all files.

OUTPUT (end)

"vocab_size": 16384,
"sha256": "<64 letters>"

Keep this file. Every dataset version and every training run uses it.
Adding or deleting files later does NOT need a new tokenizer.

---

15. Build the Training Shards

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py build-shards --input data\raw\training-data --text-field TEXT_FIELD --id-field ID_FIELD --tokenizer data\tokenizers\ored-bpe-16k-v1.json --name training-data --version VERSION --out data\tokens\training-data\VERSION --workers 8

--workers = how many CPU cores to use (number of cores minus 1 is fine).
Each Parquet file is one unit of work, so 9 files keep up to 9 cores busy.

Data split: 99% training, 1% validation, no test part. The validation part is
what decides which epoch becomes best.pt, so keep it.

OUTPUT (end)

"content_sha256": "<64 letters>",
"counts": { "documents": {...}, "tokens": {"train": ..., "val": ..., "test": ...} }

If it stops, run the same command again: it continues where it stopped.

---

16. Upload the Shards to R2

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py publish --dir data\tokens\training-data\VERSION --name training-data --version VERSION

---

17. Register the Dataset in Supabase

Step 10 first. Use the content_sha256 and token count from step 15:

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py register --name training-data --version-label VERSION --bucket ored-datasets --storage-path "training data" --dataset-type pretraining_corpus

python scripts\corpus.py update-registry --name training-data --version-label VERSION --set sha256=CONTENT_SHA256 --set token_count=TRAIN_PLUS_VAL_PLUS_TEST_TOKENS --set status=ready

After status=ready the record can no longer be changed (only deprecated).

---

18. When You Add or Delete Files

1. Add or delete the files in the R2 folder.
2. Make a fresh download folder for the new set (old files are not removed
   from an existing folder):

   python scripts\corpus.py r2-fetch --prefix "training data/" --out data\raw\training-data-VERSION --decompress

3. Step 15 with the NEW version and --reuse-from the previous one:

   python scripts\corpus.py build-shards --input data\raw\training-data-VERSION --text-field TEXT_FIELD --id-field ID_FIELD --tokenizer data\tokenizers\ored-bpe-16k-v1.json --name training-data --version VERSION --out data\tokens\training-data\VERSION --workers 8 --reuse-from data\tokens\training-data\PREVIOUS_VERSION

   Files that did not change are not tokenized again; only new files are.

4. Steps 16 and 17 with the new VERSION.
5. Keep training the same model on the new version (set DATA with the new
   VERSION first, see PART 5):

   python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml %DATA% --init-from checkpoints\ored50m\best.pt --run-name ored50m-VERSION

   It starts from the old model's weights; its own best.pt goes to
   checkpoints\ored50m-VERSION\. (--resume only works on the same version.)

