========================================
PART 5 — TRAIN
========================================

Every train command below uses the same data settings. Write them once
(VERSION = the dataset version you built in step 15):

RUN

set DATA=--set data.tokens.manifest=data\tokens\training-data\VERSION --set data.tokens.tokenizer=data\tokenizers\ored-bpe-16k-v1.json --set data.tokens.dataset_name=training-data --set data.tokens.dataset_version=VERSION

---

19. Measure What Fits on the GPU

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml --probe-batch-size

OUTPUT

{"batch_size": 1, "fits": true, "peak_gib": ..., "tokens_per_second": ...}
{"batch_size": 2, "fits": true, ...}
{"batch_size": 4, "fits": true, ...}
{"batch_size": 6, "fits": false, ...}

The default is batch 4 with 8 accumulation steps (= 32 sequences per step).
If a bigger batch fits with room to spare, e.g. 8, use half the accumulation:

--set data.batch_size=8 --set training.grad_accum_steps=4

---

20. Train

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml %DATA%

OUTPUT (start)

PRETRAINING RUN: ored50m (ored50m)
GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Laptop GPU ...
parameters    : 49,894,912
precision     : bf16
batch         : micro-batch 4 x 1024 tokens, grad accumulation 8 -> effective 32 sequences = 32,768 tokens per optimizer step
schedule      : ... steps/epoch, ... total
dataset       : training-data VERSION (content ...)

Every 1000 steps it checks the validation loss on a fixed sample of 2000
windows; if it is better, best.pt is replaced:

Epoch   1/2 step 1,000 | train loss ... | val loss ... | best ... | ... tok/s | peak ... GiB  <- new best.pt

It trains 40 epochs (40 passes over the data). For 20 epochs:

--set training.epochs=20

It stops early after 5 checks in a row (5,000 steps) without a better
validation loss, because by then the model is memorising, not learning; best.pt
keeps the best point. To never stop early:

--set training.early_stopping_patience=0

How long: the start of the run prints "schedule : ... steps/epoch" and the
log prints tok/s. Hours per epoch = steps/epoch x 32,768 / tok/s / 3600.

---

21. Continue Stopped Training

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml %DATA% --resume

It continues from the step saved in best.pt, inside the same epoch.
Steps trained after the last best.pt are trained again.

---

22. Keep best.pt in R2 Too

Step 9 first. Add this to the train command:

--set checkpoint.r2_upload=true

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml %DATA% --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true

Every new best.pt replaces ored-ai/checkpoints/ored50m/best.pt in the
ored-checkpoints bucket. Only one copy is ever kept.

---

23. If It Runs Out of GPU Memory

The run stops with:

CUDA ran out of memory with micro-batch ...

best.pt is not touched. Then either:

--set data.batch_size=2 --set training.grad_accum_steps=16

or:

--set model.gradient_checkpointing=true

and run step 20 again (or step 21 to continue).

